+### 5.9 conversation_list
+
+The server sends `conversation_list` only in reply to `list_conversations`, never as an unsolicited update.
+
+| Field           | Type                  | Description                                                   |
+| --------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`          | string                | `"conversation_list"`                                         |
+| `conversations` | ConversationSummary[] | The authenticated user's page, in newest-activity-first order |
+
+A `ConversationSummary` contains only `sessionId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, and `entryCount`; the two timestamps are ISO strings on the wire, rather than `Date` objects.
+
+- When `transport.history.enabled` is true, a list request answers outside the turn lock with the connected user's own wire-safe summaries, ignores a supplied user id, and does not send `stream_end` ([validated by: delivers only the connected user’s ISO summaries over the socket when history is enabled](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L72)).
+- With history disabled, the server answers `list_conversations` with one `error` frame carrying `UNSUPPORTED`, rather than a conversation list ([validated by: refuses a list request when history was not enabled](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L113)).
